1
00:00:00,825 --> 00:00:02,204
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:02,224 --> 00:00:06,704
Pip strokes an iron nail with Basil's magnet, again and again, always

3
00:00:06,724 --> 00:00:07,684
the same way.

4
00:00:07,954 --> 00:00:10,974
Then he holds the nail near some steel paper clips.

5
00:00:11,244 --> 00:00:12,314
What happens?

6
00:00:12,372 --> 00:00:13,892
One, nothing happens.

7
00:00:15,112 --> 00:00:17,192
Two, the nail attracts the clips.

8
00:00:18,678 --> 00:00:20,188
Hold on to your answer!

9
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:25,100
Today, we find out what the strokes did to Pip's nail!

10
00:00:25,303 --> 00:00:28,323
Our fishing game needs three hooks to catch paper fish.

11
00:00:28,353 --> 00:00:30,343
But we only have one magnet!

12
00:00:30,623 --> 00:00:33,253
A little woodpecker is hiding in this video.

13
00:00:33,513 --> 00:00:34,743
Can you spot it?

14
00:00:34,864 --> 00:00:36,594
Listen for a tap, tap, tap!

15
00:00:36,645 --> 00:00:38,105
You against the Buddies!

16
00:00:38,375 --> 00:00:40,225
Lock in first with your fingers.

17
00:00:40,495 --> 00:00:42,325
One finger for every point.

18
00:00:42,906 --> 00:00:44,226
Today you'll learn:

19
00:00:44,427 --> 00:00:46,317
What magnetised means.

20
00:00:46,514 --> 00:00:48,064
How to test the nail.

21
00:00:48,268 --> 00:00:50,068
What can be magnetised.

22
00:00:50,570 --> 00:00:51,510
Are you ready?

23
00:00:51,950 --> 00:00:52,720
Three!

24
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:53,760
Two!

25
00:00:54,130 --> 00:00:54,780
One!

26
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:55,920
Go!

27
00:00:57,309 --> 00:00:58,199
Round one!

28
00:00:58,489 --> 00:01:00,959
Pip's nail meets the steel paper clips.

29
00:01:01,239 --> 00:01:02,299
What happens?

30
00:01:02,569 --> 00:01:03,889
Show me your fingers!

31
00:01:07,363 --> 00:01:08,343
Locked in!

32
00:01:08,471 --> 00:01:09,141
One.

33
00:01:09,291 --> 00:01:12,041
The magnet has gone away now, so the nail is just a

34
00:01:12,061 --> 00:01:13,131
nail again.

35
00:01:13,182 --> 00:01:17,852
Two. An iron nail is made of a magnetic material, so it always

36
00:01:17,872 --> 00:01:19,442
attracts steel clips.

37
00:01:19,494 --> 00:01:20,124
Two!

38
00:01:20,254 --> 00:01:23,664
The hardware shop uncle strokes his screwdriver with a magnet.

39
00:01:23,844 --> 00:01:25,534
Then it holds tiny screws!

40
00:01:25,807 --> 00:01:27,097
Be the iron nail!

41
00:01:27,427 --> 00:01:28,407
Shrink down.

42
00:01:28,687 --> 00:01:29,617
Quietly.

43
00:01:31,903 --> 00:01:35,073
You are an iron nail, lying on a wooden table.

44
00:01:35,863 --> 00:01:39,163
A giant magnet comes down, onto your flat head.

45
00:01:39,673 --> 00:01:42,813
It slides all the way along you, to your sharp tip.

46
00:01:43,583 --> 00:01:46,543
Then it lifts up and away, and comes back down on your

47
00:01:46,563 --> 00:01:47,193
head.

48
00:01:47,704 --> 00:01:50,434
Again, and again, always the same way.

49
00:01:51,224 --> 00:01:54,574
Now a giant hand carries you down to the steel clips.

50
00:01:55,344 --> 00:01:57,584
They jump up, and cling to your tip!

51
00:01:59,232 --> 00:02:02,162
The answer is two: the nail attracts the clips!

52
00:02:02,412 --> 00:02:03,992
Did you show two fingers?

53
00:02:04,262 --> 00:02:05,633
Put one finger up!

54
00:02:05,653 --> 00:02:08,553
The stroke method is a way to make a magnet that uses

55
00:02:08,573 --> 00:02:13,013
a strong magnet, such as my bar magnet stroking Pip's iron nail!

56
00:02:13,742 --> 00:02:17,402
See? Iron nails always attract steel clips!

57
00:02:18,051 --> 00:02:19,201
Look closer.

58
00:02:19,791 --> 00:02:22,121
Here is a new nail from the same bag.

59
00:02:22,701 --> 00:02:24,229
Nobody has stroked it.

60
00:02:24,249 --> 00:02:26,179
Hold it over the steel clips.

61
00:02:26,759 --> 00:02:28,460
Not one clip jumps up.

62
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:33,540
Basil's magnet pulls the new nail, because iron is a magnetic material.

63
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:36,310
But the new nail is not a magnet.

64
00:02:36,330 --> 00:02:39,930
Now Pip's nail, with the magnet shut away in its box.

65
00:02:40,510 --> 00:02:41,810
The clips jump up!

66
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,150
Pip's nail has been magnetised.

67
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:49,780
Magnetised means made into a magnet, such as Pip's nail after all

68
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:50,920
those strokes!

69
00:02:53,335 --> 00:02:56,425
Pip had the right card for the wrong reason, so the Buddies

70
00:02:56,445 --> 00:02:57,545
get no point.

71
00:02:57,903 --> 00:02:59,063
Say it with me!

72
00:02:59,769 --> 00:03:03,089
When a magnetic object becomes a magnet, we say that it has

73
00:03:03,109 --> 00:03:04,599
been magnetised.

74
00:03:07,227 --> 00:03:08,127
My turn!

75
00:03:08,227 --> 00:03:10,707
I made Rod Two's hook with just one stroke.

76
00:03:10,867 --> 00:03:12,677
Look, the steel clips jump up!

77
00:03:12,801 --> 00:03:14,361
Something is not right.

78
00:03:14,631 --> 00:03:16,811
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

79
00:03:17,091 --> 00:03:18,051
Hold on!

80
00:03:23,464 --> 00:03:24,594
Arms crossed?

81
00:03:24,864 --> 00:03:26,074
One finger up!

82
00:03:26,126 --> 00:03:27,966
Look where the clips are, Basil.

83
00:03:28,246 --> 00:03:30,546
They are on your magnet, not on your nail!

84
00:03:30,746 --> 00:03:33,496
Put the magnet away first, then test the nail.

85
00:03:33,625 --> 00:03:38,035
Test the magnetised iron nail by placing it near some steel clips.

86
00:03:38,315 --> 00:03:41,595
Observe if the iron nail attracts any steel clips.

87
00:03:42,332 --> 00:03:45,672
If we stroke anything enough times, it will become a magnet.

88
00:03:45,772 --> 00:03:47,592
Even my wooden chopstick!

89
00:03:48,241 --> 00:03:49,391
Look closer.

90
00:03:49,981 --> 00:03:54,471
A copper wire, aluminium foil, a wooden chopstick and a new steel

91
00:03:54,491 --> 00:03:55,441
screwdriver.

92
00:03:56,021 --> 00:03:59,176
Before stroking, none of them attracts any clips.

93
00:03:59,196 --> 00:04:02,686
Stroke each one the same way, the same number of times.

94
00:04:03,256 --> 00:04:06,439
Now only the steel screwdriver attracts the clips.

95
00:04:06,459 --> 00:04:09,430
Steel is a magnetic material, like iron.

96
00:04:09,450 --> 00:04:12,670
A magnetic object is an object that is made of a magnetic

97
00:04:12,690 --> 00:04:16,680
material, such as an iron nail or a steel screwdriver.

98
00:04:19,980 --> 00:04:21,200
Say it with me!

99
00:04:21,908 --> 00:04:25,358
We can turn a magnetic object into a magnet by stroking it

100
00:04:25,378 --> 00:04:26,918
with a strong magnet.

101
00:04:29,396 --> 00:04:30,856
Show me your score hand!

102
00:04:31,136 --> 00:04:32,166
Two fingers?

103
00:04:32,446 --> 00:04:33,816
You beat the Buddies.

104
00:04:34,096 --> 00:04:35,096
High five!

105
00:04:35,674 --> 00:04:37,224
Did you spot the woodpecker?

106
00:04:37,544 --> 00:04:41,134
It was on the handle of a broom, outside the hardware shop!

107
00:04:41,267 --> 00:04:42,747
Here is a fun fact!

108
00:04:42,827 --> 00:04:47,107
A woodpecker pecks again and again, many times every second, like super-fast

109
00:04:47,127 --> 00:04:47,937
strokes!

110
00:04:47,957 --> 00:04:50,547
And its tongue is so long, it wraps round the back of

111
00:04:50,567 --> 00:04:51,407
its head!

112
00:04:51,532 --> 00:04:52,812
Tell someone at home!

113
00:04:53,541 --> 00:04:55,741
Let's read today's key words together!

114
00:04:56,031 --> 00:04:56,791
Ready?

115
00:04:57,078 --> 00:04:58,278
Stroke method.

116
00:04:59,879 --> 00:05:01,059
Magnetised.

117
00:05:02,648 --> 00:05:04,068
Magnetic object.

118
00:05:05,949 --> 00:05:06,889
Well done!

119
00:05:07,686 --> 00:05:08,936
My way is faster!

120
00:05:08,996 --> 00:05:11,436
Back and forth, with both ends of the magnet.

121
00:05:11,526 --> 00:05:13,160
My hook will be the strongest!

122
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:14,990
Will Basil's fast way work?

123
00:05:15,290 --> 00:05:16,870
Find out in Part Two!

124
00:05:18,028 --> 00:05:19,129
Say it with us!

125
00:05:19,929 --> 00:05:20,679
Ready?

126
00:05:20,803 --> 00:05:21,463
One!

127
00:05:21,803 --> 00:05:22,503
two!

128
00:05:22,808 --> 00:05:23,983
Now you know!
